tion":"history of art","english":"history of art","bold_translation_offsets":[[11,14]],"type":"example"},{"text":"bildende Kunst","bold_text_offsets":[[9,14]],"translation":"visual arts","english":"visual arts","bold_translation_offsets":[[7,11]],"type":"example"},{"text":"die sieben freien Künste","bold_text_offsets":[[18,24]],"translation":"the seven liberal arts","english":"the seven liberal arts","bold_translation_offsets":[[18,22]],"type":"example"},{"text":"Wer für den Einfluß der Kunst empfänglich ist, weiß ihn als Lustquelle und Lebenströstung nicht hoch genug einzuschätzen.","ref":"1930, Sigmund Freud, Das Unbehagen in der Kultur [Civilization and Its Discontents], Vienna: Internationaler Psychoanalytischer Verlag:","english":"Civilization and Its Discontents","type":"quotation","translation":"Civilization and Its Discontents","bold_text_offsets":[[24,29]]},{"text":"Der Versuch des Mannes, die Frau zu ergründen, ist seit Jahrtausenden gescheitert. Das immer wieder zu versuchen liegt an der einfachen Konstruktion seines Hirns, das das Unmögliche nicht als unmöglich begreifen kann. Die Versuche misslangen, die Versuchung blieb, und daraus wurde Kunst.","ref":"2001, Jurij Brězan, edited by Lucia Heine, Ze studnje lět/Brunnen der Jahre: Zběrka sentencow, aforistiskich myslow a zapisow/Eine Sammlung von Sentenzen, aphoristischen Gedanken und Notaten, 1st edition, Budyšin/Bautzen: Ludowe nakładnistwo Domowina/Domowina-Verlag, →ISBN, German section, page 61:","english":"Man’s attempt to fathom women has failed for millennia. To still go on making these attempts is due to the simple construction of his brain that cannot grasp the impossible as impossible. The attempts failed, the temptation abode, and thus turned into art.","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[282,287]],"translation":"Man’s attempt to fathom women has failed for millennia. To still go on making these attempts is due to the simple construction of his brain that cannot grasp the impossible as impossible. The attempts failed, the temptation abode, and thus turned into art.","bold_translation_offsets":[[252,255]]}],"categories":["German countable nouns","German terms with quotations","German terms with usage examples","German uncountable nouns","Requests for translations of German quotations"],"links":[["art","art"]],"raw_glosses":["(uncountable, countable) art"],"glosses":["art"],"tags":["countable","feminine","uncountable"]},{"examples":[{"text":"Kunstsammler","bold_text_offsets":[[0,5]],"translation":"art collector","english":"art collector","bold_translation_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example"},{"text":"Diese Woche wird im Museum mittelalterliche Kunst ausgestellt.","bold_text_offsets":[[44,49]],"translation":"This week, medieval works of art are on display in the museum.","english":"This week, medieval works of art are on display in the museum.","bold_translation_offsets":[[20,32]],"type":"example"}],"categories":["German collective nouns","German terms with usage examples","German uncountable nouns"],"links":[["artwork","artwork"],["works of art","work of art"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Kunstwerke"}],"raw_glosses":["(uncountable, collectively) artworks, works of art"],"glosses":["artworks, works of art"],"tags":["collective","feminine","uncountable"]},{"examples":[{"text":"die Kunst des Kochens","bold_text_offsets":[[4,9]],"translation":"the craft of cooking","english":"the craft of cooking","bold_translation_offsets":[[4,9]],"type":"example"},{"text":"keine Kunst sein","bold_text_offsets":[[6,11]],"translation":"to not be a feat","english":"to not be a feat","bold_translation_offsets":[[12,16]],"literal_meaning":"to not be a craft","bold_literal_offsets":[[12,17]],"type":"example"}],"info_templates":[{"args":{"1":"de","2":"gen<of something>"},"name":"+obj","extra_data":{"words":["genitive","‘of","something’"]},"expansion":"[with genitive ‘of something’]"}],"links":[["craft","craft"]],"raw_glosses":["(usually accompanied by a genitive or adjective or as part 